    "notes": "Weights: openbmb/MiniCPM5-2B at 12a3808a956f869c767195e9266b59c4d21d92e2, BF16, sha256 checked against the Hub. Speculative decoding with the card-recommended DSpark drafter openbmb/MiniCPM5-2B-DSpark at 114a20fdbf53220712c7fbdd7dccddbf1dedebb4 (BF16, 5 layers, 324M parameters, 0.65 GB), --speculative-algorithm DSPARK --speculative-dspark-block-size 7 as in the model card. SGLang 0.5.20 from PyPI in a Python 3.12 venv (uv) with torch 2.13.0+cu130, flashinfer-python 0.6.18, sglang-kernel 0.4.7, triton 3.7.1, transformers 5.12.1, xgrammar 0.2.1; CUDA 13.0, driver 580.173.02, Ubuntu 24.04.4, kernel 6.17.0-1029-nvidia. Environment SGLANG_ALLOW_OVERWRITE_LONGER_CONTEXT_LEN=1 and SGLANG_DISABLE_CUDNN_CHECK=1 as the MiniCPM SGLang cookbook recommends, the venv bin directory on PATH (flashinfer JIT needs ninja). Server flags follow the openbmb SGLang cookbook (docs/deployment/sglang.md): --dtype bfloat16 --context-length 131072 --tool-call-parser minicpm5, plus --reasoning-parser qwen3 so the <think> block lands in reasoning_content; --mem-fraction-static 0.75 instead of the cookbook 0.85 to leave the unified-memory box about 20 GB of host headroom (the KV pool still holds about 2 million tokens). Radix prefix cache, chunked prefill 8192, CUDA graphs and the flashinfer attention backend are SGLang defaults. Every request sets temperature 0 and seed 42 as the workloads specify. The chat template has three thinking states: enable_thinking true prefills <think>, false prefills an empty think block, and unset lets the model decide, which on almost every prompt means it thinks. Speed and long-context depth rows send chat_template_kwargs enable_thinking false; eval and needle rows leave it unset (the template default). Load: target weights 36.8 s (5.01 GB) plus the DSpark drafter 3.5 s (0.93 GB, loaded as Qwen3DSparkModel), KV allocation 3.6 s, CUDA graphs prefill 17.4 s / target-verify 2.5 s / draft-decode 1.7 s, scheduler end to end 71.2 s; SGLang reported max_total_num_tokens 1,798,013 (down from the plain 2B's 2,034,852 because the drafter and the verify buffers take their share) and 22.7 GB of GPU memory still free. max_running_requests is passed explicitly as 512 and confirmed at 512 from /get_server_info before the first concurrent row."
  },
